{
  "_comment": "THE BODY SITE REGISTER — SHA, 2026-09-12. The one vocabulary of physical places on a body. Five chamber sessions choose WHERE the fork goes by five different systems (natal chart, anatomical ladder, feet-up sweep, chakra centres, marma points); each of those systems names the same places differently, so a photograph keyed to any one of them is wrong in the other four. This file is the join. A photograph shows A PLACE ON A BODY — the system is only the reason you chose that place. So imagery, anchors and captions key here, and each system supplies only its own reason.",
  "_discipline": "Every site carries the discipline the body itself demands: contact (stem may rest), field (tines float clear), fieldOnly (never touched, swept only). The engine may TIGHTEN this per person and never loosens it. A contact photograph may never appear on a step that resolved to a sweep — that gate is mechanical, not a judgement call.",
  "_order": "Listed crown to sole by the anchor y each site already carried, so the register reads as the body reads.",
