  "_chakraNote": "The Sacral centre and the Root resolve to the lower belly and the tail bone — both field-only, per SHA's standing ruling that the reproductive region and the coccyx are swept and never touched. Their marma doorways (Kati on the sacrum, Trik at the tail bone) remain available as labelled alternates worked from behind; they are never the headline placement, because a centre named on the front of the body must not silently move to the back.",
